3️⃣ Let’s code a method boost in our RaceService. The method will receive a raceId and a ponyId,
    and will call the backend API (https://ponyracer.ninja-squad.com/apidoc#resources-boost)
    race-service.ts:

        boost(raceId: number, ponyId: number): Observable<void> {
            return this.http.post<void>(`${environment.baseUrl}/api/races/${raceId}/boosts`, { ponyId });
        }


4️⃣ Now we need to trigger this boost. Here is the broad picture: we want to boost a pony if a
    player has clicked at least 5 times over a second on a pony. RxJS and a few of its operators
    will help us to achieve that.

    🔥We need to start listening to the ponySelected event emitted by our ponies when we click on
    them. Add a method onSelection in our Live. This method will receive the pony clicked and
    should be called when a ponySelected event arises during a running race.

    🔥Create a field in the component called clickSubject, of type Subject<PonyWithPositionModel>,
    and initialize it with a new Subject. The onSelection method should simply emit the received
    pony with clickSubject.

    live.html:

        @case ('RUNNING') {
            // omitted
            <pr-pony [ponyModel]="pony" [isRunning]="true" [isBoosted]="pony.boosted" 
            👉(ponySelected)="onSelection(pony)"/>     
        }

    live.ts:

        protected readonly clickSubject = new Subject<PonyWithPositionModel>();
        protected onSelection(pony: PonyWithPositionModel): void {
            this.clickSubject.next(pony);
        }

    🔥🔥We now have a stream of clicks, that we need to transform to only call the boost method
    of the RaceService if we have at least 5 clicks on the same pony in less than a second.



5️⃣ We now have a stream of clicks, that we need to transform to only call the boost method of the
    RaceService if we have at least 5 clicks on the same pony in less than a second.

    🔥A simple way to do that is to keep the recent clicks in memory. 🔥🔥RxJS offers the timestamp
    operator, which wraps each click with the instant when it occurred. That gives us enough
    information to compute a sliding window of recent clicks.

    🔥🔥We can then use scan to build an array containing only the recent clicks for the current
    pony. For each new click:
        👉 if we already have 5 clicks stored, we reset the accumulator with the latest click;
        👉otherwise, we add the new click and keep only the clicks on the same pony, emitted less
        than one second ago
    
    This means that mixed clicks on several ponies do not count together: 2 clicks on pony1, then
    2 on pony2, then 3 on pony1 will still only count as 3 recent clicks on pony1.

    🔥🔥Once the accumulator reaches 5 elements, we know we have 5 clicks on the same pony within
    the last second. We can then:
        👉 filter to keep only the arrays of length 5;
        👉 map to extract the pony ID from the first stored click;
        👉 switchMap to call the boost method.
    
    As we don’t need the value returned by boost, we can simply end with .subscribe();.

    The call to boost can fail, though. If we don’t handle this error, the whole stream stops
    listening forever. Add a catchError operator after the boost call and return EMPTY.

        this.clickSubject
        .pipe(
            timestamp(),
            scan((acc: Array<Timestamp<PonyWithPositionModel>>, click) => {
            if (acc.length === 5) {
                return [click];
            } else {
                return [...acc, click]
                .filter(c => c.value.id === click.value.id && c.timestamp > click.timestamp - 1000);
            }
            }, []),
            filter(clicks => clicks.length === 5),
            map(clicks => clicks[0].value.id),
            switchMap(ponyId => this.raceService.boost(this.raceModel()!.id, ponyId).pipe(catchError(() => EMPTY)))
        )
        .subscribe();
    
    ✅When that’s done you can try to click 5 times quickly on a pony during a race: that should
    trigger a request to our backend. The next poniesWithPosition received will contain the boosted
    pony with a true value in its boosted attribute, and thus we should have a pony with a beautiful
    rainbow!



