😵‍💫Confusion with the await vi.advanceTimersByTimeAsync(50);

    👉 It advances the fake clock to a from 0 to all the way to 50ms.
    👉 For clarity assume the followind code:

        (👇this represents the starting line of the test file mockRaceResource of live.spec.ts)
        of('Hello').pipe(
            delay(5)
        ).subscribe(() => {
            console.log('Received');
        });

        await vi.advanceTimersByTimeAsync(10);  // test
    
    1) of('Hello') 
        -> Observable is created

    2) .pipe(delay(5))
        -> RxJS says "Before I emit 'Hello', wait 5 milliseconds."
    
    3) .subscribe(...)
        -> Observable starts running.
        -> delay(5) timer is started.
        -> nothing has been emitted yet.
    
    4) await vi.advanceTimersByTimeAsync(10);
        -> Now test executes
        -> This says "Move the fake clock from 0 ms all the way to 10 ms."
        -> 🔥Notice we're not instantly jumping to 10 ms. Vitest moves through time and checks
            every timer along the way.
        -> 🔥While moving from 0 ms → 10 ms, Vitest reaches 5 ms. It notices:
            delay(5) has expired.
            So it immediately executes it. That causes RxJS to emit: "Hello"
    
    5) The subscriber receives the value.

            .subscribe(() => {
                console.log('Received');
            });

        -> Now this runs. and "Received" is logged
    
    6) 🔥Vitest isn't finished yet.
        -> Even though the delay(5) timer has fired, you asked it to advance to 10 ms.
            So it continues moving:

                6 ms
                7 ms
                8 ms
                9 ms
                10 ms

        -> 🔥It looks for more timers. There aren't any. So it stops.
        -> Final state:
                Current fake time: 10 ms
                No pending timers.
    
    
    🧠 Timeline:

            0 ms
            │
            ├── delay(5) starts waiting
            │
            ├── advanceTimersByTimeAsync(10)
            │
            ├── reaches 5 ms
            │      │
            │      ├── delay timer expires
            │      ├── Observable emits "Hello"
            │      └── subscribe callback runs
            │
            ├── continues...
            │
            ├── 6 ms
            ├── 7 ms
            ├── 8 ms
            ├── 9 ms
            │
            └── reaches 10 ms